    <CATEGORY Name="Recording">
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl1_01_01">Bienvenue, ye be now listenin' to the sound o' me disembodied voice. It will serve ye no purpose to look fer me, fer this a voice from the past.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl1_01_02">I bid ye welcome to me cabinet o' perturbation. It be me study o' the human psyche - specifically yers. A set o' recordings have been prepared to chaperone ye through the chambers ahead.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl1_01_03">There be a few parts to this study and it be up to ye - not only to pass, but figure out what elements be important. Please go on, move into the next chamber.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl1_01_04">Just remember they can all be saved, there be always a way.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl1_02_01">Congratulations fer comin' this far, I be so excited fer ye. Yo ho ho, I do hope ye managed to save Monsieur Fournier. He was a matey and a colleague o' me papa, ye know.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl1_02_02">Friendly fellow, a real bon garçon, but frail o' mind. He puts up an impressive front, but it be all an act, I assure. Please go on, we be just gettin' started.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl2_01_01">On this next piece ye should be lookin' fer some divine inspiration. Time to delve into yer spiritual side. What do ye see? Be the man beggin' fer mercy or be he bein' blessed.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl2_01_02">Perhaps both! Father used to say, there were no right answers. Have the light guide ye.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl2_02_01">I wonder, be Father David with his God now? Maybe ye helped him there. Blimey, don't ye worry, I be sure he didn't have a family, he probably wasn't even all that well-liked.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl2_02_02">With the current political climate, I be surprised someone hadn't killed him already. Avast, we can't all be saved. Some doesn't even want to be saved. Aye. That be a comfortin' thought.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl2_02_03">Saves us from tryin'.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl3_01_01">Shiver me timbers, I be sure ye have figured out how it all works by now. Be ye enjoyin' me quips? I think they be quite clever.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl3_01_02">Not that I ever was much o' conversationalist, poetry has always been me forte.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl3_01_03">But I digress. Ye should press on, it will all be over soon, arr. Also, the police be here, maybe they can help ye.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl3_02_01">Inspector Marot, be ye still with us? I be lookin' forward to see if ye managed to save him or not. I know mighty little about him, but surely he had a family, don't ye think?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl3_02_02">Poor, poor, fatherless children. But he falls on his own sword. His kind be not meant to come fer people like me. Laws be made fer cretins.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl3_02_03">The aristocracy doesn't need to know right from wrong. We be always right.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl4_01_01">Well done. Ye have triumphed - conquered me cabinet. I wish I could tell ye how ye did, but alas this be a recordin'. Ye will have to figure it out all by yerself.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl4_01_02">Did anyone survive? The doctor? The priest? Or perhaps the police man. Who was allowed to live? Why?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl4_01_03">Ye should really reflect on these past events and consider what they meant to ye, what ye have learned about yer true nature.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl4_01_04">Father never knew me. He thought he did, but then he was frightened and nothin' was ever the same again. I can still see him, lyin' there on the deck, he looked so surprised.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl4_01_05">-- The star-shaped soapstone stained by his blood, fell to the deck with a sonorous thud. Blame me not fer I was but a child, with careful ambition I dared a smile. --</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl4_01_06">Rest in peace, papa.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="justine_rec_lvl4_02_01">And so it comes to an end. Now that ye have seen what ye truly be, ye be able to go on and face eternity without fear - without doubt.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="brokenrec_justine_01">... speak into the phonograph, Basile, mon chéri.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="brokenrec_basile_02">... what did ye put into the rum?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="brokenrec_justine_03">Absinthe, silly Basile, strong men like ye don't drink rum - rum be fer helpless women like meself.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="brokenrec_basile_04">Me head, what be this thing, get me out. Blimey, I be not up fer yer games.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="brokenrec_justine_05">Nay, ye have to say it first. Yarr, how beautiful be I?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="brokenrec_basile_06">Plenty, now let me out o' this thing?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="brokenrec_justine_07">Nay, that be not what ye say!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="brokenrec_basile_08">Yer beauty be blindin'.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="brokenrec_basile_09">Me eyes! What have ye done to me eyes!?</Entry>
        <Entry Name="brokenrec_basile_10">Justine this ain't funny, ye blinded me!</Entry>
        <Entry Name="brokenrec_justine_11">Avast, ye can't catch me now.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="brokenrec_basile_12">I'll kill ye, ye whore!</Entry>
