    <CATEGORY Name="L04Final">
        <Entry Name="AngelStatue">"What was mother like?"[br][br]"She was the most beautiful creature ever to grace this world."[br][br]"I can't remember what she looked like, no matter how hard I try."[br][br]"Her beauty was blindin', Justine. We could never dare to chain such memory to our minds. It would be too much to bear."</Entry>
        <Entry Name="FatherGrave">It all made sense, he thought, we all appreciate symmetry. Everyone be comforted by the causality o' logic. It gives the impression o' a grand plan and that we may be able to grasp the inner workings o' this perfect universe.[br][br]Ye see, his wife had died while givin' birth to his son. Avast, that be why he was able to forgive. His family was just givin' in to the symmetry.</Entry>
    </CATEGORY>
    <CATEGORY Name="LoadingText">
        <Entry Name="Load02_01">The basement had been extended well beyond the manor durin' the time o' the first revolution. Justine was not to enter without permission, but now there was no one left to ask.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Load02_02">The gloomy space downstairs became a playground - a mysterious place fer Justine to discover with her mateys.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Load02_03">The downstairs library still reminded her o' father. All them hours spent there had fostered a sense o' shelter.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Load03_01">They knew that they would have to capture the men, but what to ultimately do with 'em, was a decision that had to be postponed.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Load03_02">Abacinatin' the suitors had not been a part o' the original plan, but she liked the added excitement.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Load03_03">Justine was not a person who would go about plannin'. The Cabinet came about as her whimsy collided with other people's misfortune.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Load04_01">Could it be that she was not herself anymore, she thought. Blimey, it was time to find out.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Load04_02">Justine had overdosed on Lithium before and had a pretty good idea o' what effects to expect.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="Load04_03">Har har, when she first imagined the cabinet, it was fer her amusement, but since it had grown into somethin' more important - an opportunity to reveal her most suppressed desires.</Entry>
    </CATEGORY>
    <CATEGORY Name="PreMenu">
        <Entry Name="PTestWelcome01">Good o' ye to come. This time it will be a trial o' character.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="PTestWelcome02">Bear in mind. Death be final - nothin' will be saved.</Entry>
        <Entry Name="PTestWelcome03">Arr, come on, wake up. Ye need to get goin'.</Entry>
    </CATEGORY>
